{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel journeyed from Be'erot Benei Ya'akan to Moserah.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory asked: did they journey from Be'erot Benei Ya'akan to Moserah? Was it not rather from Moserah that they came to Benei Ya'akan, as it says (Numbers 33): ״ויסעו ממוסרות ויחנו בבני יעקן״? And furthermore, what of what it says here, ״שם מת אהרן ויקבר שם״ — 'Aharon died there and was buried there'? Did Aharon die in Moserah? Did he not die at Hor HaHar? For we find eight journeys from Moserah to Hor HaHar. Rather, the meaning of the verse ״שם מת אהרן ויקבר שם״ is: in Moserah the children of Israel made a great mourning as though Aharon had died and been buried there. And this too is part of the rebuke. He said to them: at the end of forty years, when Aharon died at Hor HaHar and the clouds of glory departed, they feared the battle against the Canaanite and said, ״נתנה ראש״ and so on, and they turned back toward Egypt eight journeys. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that the children of Levi fought against them at that time when they said thus, and killed many of them; and because of this they made a great mourning in Moserah." "<b>And why</b> was this rebuke juxtaposed to the breaking of the tablets? To teach you that the death of the righteous is as difficult as the breaking of the tablets. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Isaiah 29): ״הנני יוסיף להפליא את העם הזה הפלא ופלא ואבדה חכמת חכמיו״ and so on — the departure of the sages of Israel is twice as severe as the destruction of the Holy Temple, for in all the curses in Mishneh Torah only one הפלאה is mentioned, as it says (Deuteronomy 28): ״והפלא ה׳ את מכותך״, whereas here there are two, as it says (Isaiah 29): ״הפלא ופלא ואבדה חכמת חכמיו״ and so on."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:13.496708274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}